WEBVTT

00:09:59.810 --> 00:10:03.146
that sense that it's safe to
kind of speak up in the group.

00:10:03.170 --> 00:10:05.751
It can lead to people
withholding information

00:10:05.775 --> 00:10:07.497
rather than sharing what they know,

00:10:07.521 --> 00:10:08.756
it can increase conflict.

00:10:08.780 --> 00:10:12.426
And so it's really important
of the team leader

00:10:12.450 --> 00:10:16.696
to articulate for an overarching goal.

00:10:16.720 --> 00:10:19.839
AG: Goal-setting isn't usually
the first thing that comes to mind

00:10:19.863 --> 00:10:21.496
when thinking about team identity.

00:10:21.520 --> 00:10:24.796
What most people try instead
is team-building activities.

00:10:24.820 --> 00:10:27.079
I'm guessing you've
suffered through Zoom calls

00:10:27.103 --> 00:10:29.668
where you're asked to name
your favorite pizza topping

00:10:29.692 --> 00:10:33.136
or to share highlights from your totally
boring weekend in quarantine.